Question: During the post-mortem discussion, what specific operational policy did alice mandate to prevent similar confusion in future feature rollouts?

Asking Claude...
Based on the processed data, here's the answer:

## Answer

During the post-mortem discussion on **January 19, 2025**, **Alice** mandated the following operational policy:

**"All internal team members must be explicitly assigned to specific test groups rather than random distribution."**

This policy was established to prevent debugging confusion in future feature rollouts. The issue arose because team members were randomly bucketed into different test groups (30% new algorithm, 70% old algorithm), which made them unknowingly experience different system behaviors during debugging. This created "parallel realities" that made internal investigation nearly impossible until they realized the feature flag was working as intended.

**Reference**: /workspace/config_vg_3_company_context/09_activity_streams/slack_threads/engineering.md (line 62-63) and daily_digests/2025-01-19.md (line 22-23)

